            "review_title": "Review at Lavelle Library",
            "review_text": "Dominique D\nHanoi, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nA charming place, expensive and sadly desapointing\nNov 2021\nTuesday, 10.30 am, I was there for a ice coffee. 100K VND (4 dollars) quite expensive isn't it ? a charming waiter bebore directing me or placing me in the room, asked me what i desired to have then desapeared. So as a guest, I chose a spot in an empty room. \nI ordered for a black ice coffee in my isotherm contenant ( that i always have with me) then started to work. The same waiter brought my coffee. As i asked for a cup of ice water, he politely answered that the house didn't do that. I was a bit shocking, a coffee with a price five times more expensive than any ordinary cafe, at least I could have a glass of water, since 20L of mineral water \"la vie\" is about 60K VND. \nAS, I certainly did an \"ugly face\" at that moment, this charming waiter served me this asked suplement water. \nStill the place is charming, there is a lot of green. Exuberant exotic plants are everywhere so the coffee seems worth the price. \nHowever, I should come back another time of the day. Guests here for the lunch time are quite noisy and working is quite difficult. earplugs are needed.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 23, 2021",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
